@startuml
title Book Room - Smart Campus Study Room Booking

actor Student
participant BookingService
database BookingRepository

Student -> BookingService: bookRoom(roomId, startTime, endTime)
activate BookingService

BookingService -> BookingService: validate future start time
BookingService --> Student: validation result

alt Rules valid
    BookingService -> BookingService: check room is unblocked
    BookingService -> BookingRepository: findAvailableRoom(roomId, startTime, endTime)
    activate BookingRepository

    BookingRepository --> BookingService: room available
    deactivate BookingRepository

    BookingService -> BookingRepository: saveBooking(studentId, roomId, startTime, endTime)
    activate BookingRepository

    BookingRepository --> BookingService: booking created
    deactivate BookingRepository

    BookingService --> Student: Booking confirmed

else Room unavailable or rules invalid
    BookingService --> Student: Room unavailable / booking rejected
    Student -> BookingService: request alternative room
    BookingService -> BookingRepository: findAvailableRooms(startTime, endTime)
    activate BookingRepository

    BookingRepository --> BookingService: available rooms
    deactivate BookingRepository

    BookingService --> Student: Alternative rooms returned
end

deactivate BookingService

note right of BookingService
Design component:
BookingService contains booking
validation and application logic.

It checks:
- room is unblocked
- start time is in the future
- booking does not conflict
- R2 duration rule
- R3 overlap rule
end note

note right of BookingRepository
Design component:
BookingRepository handles persistence
and searches for available rooms
and existing bookings.
end note

note bottom
Assumptions:
1. Student is already authenticated.
2. BookingService is responsible for enforcing
   the approved booking rules.
3. BookingRepository can detect conflicting
   bookings for the selected room.
4. A rejected booking is not saved.
5. An alternative room search uses the same
   requested time interval.
6. R2 and R3 are applied according to the
   project's approved rules.
end note

@enduml